                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2961c5e1-01a2-37cc-a4d2-0af1bf35ed8f",
                        "entry_id": "3b27cf11-ba2c-3e52-b3dd-6dda9407c3f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "собир. женские украшения не из драгоценных камней и металлов"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "107d9d64-eca6-3b15-ab4a-61fab1c6376d",
                        "entry_id": "3b27cf11-ba2c-3e52-b3dd-6dda9407c3f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "собир. перен. о различных предметах специального назначения, сопровождающих какую-либо деятельность"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "98cdc5a3-6c11-4e01-950a-0eeb1ca64f24",
                                "sense_id": "107d9d64-eca6-3b15-ab4a-61fab1c6376d",
                                "text": "Сегодня уже глупо полагать майки, ручки с клубным лого, видеокассеты с голами и прочую футбольную бижутерию милым пустяком."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e5880020-043b-32bd-ac24-342427100a9b",
                        "entry_id": "3b27cf11-ba2c-3e52-b3dd-6dda9407c3f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. о том, что имитирует что-либо, создаёт видимость чего-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3b82eff0-040e-4a60-a6a2-a2fbc3a1043c",
                        "source_entry_id": "3b27cf11-ba2c-3e52-b3dd-6dda9407c3f3",
                        "target_lang_word": "bijouterie",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bijouterie",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "13f5954c-4078-30a6-864f-0c5f6e6393bf",
                                        "entry_id": "8e943079-9bdf-3311-8940-1e9c4e880ee1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Small articles of jewellery, trinkets, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77a8ff42-2008-451e-a95c-d43176d632dd",
                                                "sense_id": "13f5954c-4078-30a6-864f-0c5f6e6393bf",
                                                "text": "Is not Howel and James's shop filled with all that human art can invent, or human taste display—bijouterie touched with present sentiment, or radiant with future triumph?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a5ad423-91b2-4032-bd17-7e410326d90b",
                                                "sense_id": "13f5954c-4078-30a6-864f-0c5f6e6393bf",
                                                "text": "The finer kinds of perfumery, prettily cut-glass bottles, and all sorts of bijouterie for the toilet or drawing-room table, good plaister casts, and in fact every thing ornamental, as far as the pecuniary means can afford, should be taken."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b1e0fb1-38b5-4698-8c0f-2efe9dc6cace",
                                                "sense_id": "13f5954c-4078-30a6-864f-0c5f6e6393bf",
                                                "text": "The first objects to attract attention are the large stands in the centre of the hall containing Mr. Simonton's brilliant display of bronze, painted china, and pretty bijouterie; the exquisite laces of Forrest and Allen; and the large collection of preparations for the toilet exhibited by Fred. Lewis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8f535e0-4321-4bef-a4c8-2817c4ab15bd",
                                                "sense_id": "13f5954c-4078-30a6-864f-0c5f6e6393bf",
                                                "text": "The women cultivate and plant the ground, and after feeding their husbands, expend the surplus products in the beads and baubles which compose their bijouterie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8735d414-00bb-4b2c-8c48-a13e7954c98e",
                        "source_entry_id": "3b27cf11-ba2c-3e52-b3dd-6dda9407c3f3",
                        "target_lang_word": "costume jewellery",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
